  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5901.11 Call jumping",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5901.11 “Call jumping” means the unauthorized response to or transport of a patient pursuant to an emergency medical services call in which a unit or provider was not directly called, dispatched, or requested to assist.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 and Revision Note #2 at Chapter heading for Saf-C 5900) #12790, eff 5-24-19",
